        "id": 227423,
        "name": "The Mariner",
        "username": "The_Mariner",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_mariner/{size}/2025_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-05-12T00:25:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If more than one makes it then a series of Ultimate difficulty runoffs, alternating between solo and Vengeance mode, will go until one or none of the teams are left. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>EDIT: Team 2 is actually amazing. &nbsp;After a few turns, all three heroes were consistently able to either play, power, or draw on both of the other heroes’ turn. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>By the way, Round 1 is over. &nbsp;Apostate and Dok’Thorath aren’t bad on their own, but they work together a little too well, and with my mediocre skills, teams 3, 6, 8, 10, and 11 were eliminated. &nbsp;Without exception, these battles were close, but fighting the long game against Apostate with one hero left standing is rarely recommended, and that’s what happened to each of those.</p>\n<p>EDIT: 3 games in, 3 teams are left: The Harbingers, The Prophets, and the Keepers. &nbsp;Round 2 went smoothly- Chokepoint is a cakewalk- but the Matriarch tripped up 3 of the 6 remaining teams.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:01:37.309Z",
